WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.200
- [Reporter] Your character gets stranded

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.581
out at sea
(smooching on kitten)

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:03.414
with her boyfriend.
- And I'm just

00:00:03.414 --> 00:00:04.626
a little busy making out with a cat.

00:00:04.626 --> 00:00:06.106
(laughing)

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:10.567
(whooshing)
(upbeat music)

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.398
Who wants to hang out with me (laughing)?

00:00:12.398 --> 00:00:14.731
(whooshing)

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.490
I should probably say my boyfriend

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.640
but I feel like after
having been stuck at sea

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:26.330
with Sam for 41 days, and
having witnessed what,

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.100
how we were able to support one another,

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.790
I would first say my boyfriend

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.040
and then I would say Sam.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.530
Okay, you can run free and I'll bug

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:33.730
one of your friends now.

00:00:33.869 --> 00:00:36.202
(whooshing)

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.947
I feel like I would, I don't know,

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.630
I think I'd maybe, oh,

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.750
I think one of the cats just pooed.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.910
I think I'd maybe be a teacher.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:54.700
I really like the idea
of, of shaping young minds

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.050
and inspiring them to be
anything that they wanna be

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:59.240
and encouraging growth through education.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.892
(whooshing)

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.160
It's important to have a good strong sense

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:07.480
of identity and self

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:10.840
and to not take anything too seriously.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.560
I think throughout growing
up in this industry

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.980
it's all too easy to give your power away

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:18.210
and to let others
opinions really affect you

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.850
in a deep way, but yeah,
I think it's important

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.720
to constantly try and
understand who you are

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:27.250
outside of the labels in
which others either give you

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:28.600
or you design for yourself.

00:01:28.791 --> 00:01:31.124
(whooshing)

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.570
Maybe we could make like
an adult swim version of

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:37.350
Secret Life of the American Teenager,

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.183
I might consider that,

00:01:38.183 --> 00:01:39.850
I think that would be a funny (laughing),

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:40.980
funny spinoff.

00:01:41.647 --> 00:01:43.980
(whooshing)

00:01:44.666 --> 00:01:46.520
I do keep in touch with some
of the cast from Secret Life.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.340
Megan Park and I, who
played Grace on the show,

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.450
are still extremely close

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.190
and I actually had a
dream a couple weeks ago

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:54.680
about the whole cast and that we all had

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:55.980
this little reunion dinner

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.770
and so I think Megan, I told her about it

00:01:58.770 --> 00:01:59.890
and she reached out to Francia

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:00.960
and I reached out to a couple

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:01.800
of the other cast members

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.820
and I think hopefully we might do a cast,

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:04.770
a cast dinner soon.

00:02:04.849 --> 00:02:07.182
(whooshing)

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.120
Team Ricky, all the way.

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:10.830
- [Reporter] Why's that?

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:13.370
- I mean I just feel like he came around.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:15.310
He discovered that he wasn't perhaps

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:17.620
the most supportive
father in the beginning

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:19.640
but recognized his mistakes

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:20.720
and I'm all about forgiveness

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.920
and I'd like to think that
if I were in Amy's shoes

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.750
I would find forgiveness in order

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:29.500
to create a happy little
family for my child.

00:02:30.045 --> 00:02:32.378
(whooshing)

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:37.400
I feel like I'd get along
probably best with Tami actually,

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.690
the character from the movie
that I just did, Adrift,

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:40.580
simply because we both

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:41.910
have really adventurous spirits

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:45.030
and are very keen on exploring the world.

00:02:45.071 --> 00:02:47.404
(whooshing)

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.560
I'd like to visit every
single onsen in Japan

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.600
which is probably completely unattainable

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.780
and an insane bucket list item

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.810
but I'm a huge fan of hot springs

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.060
and the Japanese culture

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:01.090
and that's something that
I would like to achieve

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.098
one day before I die (laughing).

00:03:03.098 --> 00:03:05.431
(whooshing)

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:10.870
I think that, you know, it's
one thing to sign a petition

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:13.100
or to retweet something,
it's another thing

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.900
to actually take definitive
steps to create change, and.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.940
When we think about change
we think that we have

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.630
to do something on a really big level

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:22.020
in order to create a lot of progress

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.380
but often times change can be very simple

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.560
and it doesn't have to be huge.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.933
(whooshing)

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.470
Oh gosh, I would get in so much trouble

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:35.170
for talking a lot about it.
(reporter laughing)

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:37.460
For me personally I
can't wait to see, what,

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.390
you know, Meryl Streep continues to do.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:41.720
Just working with her is so outstanding

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.127
and spectacular and
something I never thought

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.200
that'd I'd have the opportunity to do

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:51.200
and she really is, my
gosh they're so cute,

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.970
she really is the most dynamic actress

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:57.250
and raises the bar for every single person

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.824
in her presence to be a better artist.

00:03:59.824 --> 00:04:02.157
(whooshing)

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.610
Oh, honestly I'm all about that,

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:07.020
like joy life at the moment.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:09.870
Just frikin' laugh a lot and find the joy

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:12.230
in every moment and I think
you look the most beautiful.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.140
I do love makeup and I love putting on

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:15.790
some red lips every now and then.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:19.010
I've been really into this
brand at the moment called,

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:21.610
Pinch of Colour, I think
it's Pinch of Color actually.

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.830
And they make all of their
products without any water

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.940
so all their lipsticks
and their concealers

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:27.990
have no water in them
which is really sustainable

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.100
and really good for the earth.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.433
(whooshing)

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.360
I mean, never say never.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.570
You know, I think it's a long life to live

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:41.600
and depending on which way
our politics continue to go

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:43.650
maybe I'll feel, there's a
guy hiding right behind me,

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.900
I think we're playing
hide-and-seek, found you.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.420
I think there's a lot of opportunity

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.920
for change and I don't
know if I'll be a supporter

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.140
of others running for a long time to come

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:53.820
or if I'll be running myself one day

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:55.480
but I would never say never.

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:57.650
All these little guys are from

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.410
Best Friends Animal Society

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.460
and they're doing such incredible work

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:03.490
to save the lives of
thousands of little kitties

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:06.410
and puppies and you
can adopt one yourself.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.730
I'm probably gonna take one
of these guys home today.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:13.610
You can go to bestfriends.org
to adopt a puppy or a kitty.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.910
I just think it's
wonderful to support people

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.450
who are doing good work
for other creatures

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.440
on this planet, so, check 'em out!

00:05:24.586 --> 00:05:27.108
(whooshing)
(sign squeaking)

